paired, n = 50 MLPs   (v2.4.1 graded vs tail-regressing candidate)
  mean score          v2.4.1 graded: 2.631432e-07   tail-regressing candidate: 2.650692e-07
  PRIMARY  arithmetic mean difference (ctrl - cand, >0 = candidate better)
      delta            -1.926031e-09
      relative         -0.732%   (gain 0.9927x)
      bootstrap 95% CI [-2.1291e-08, +8.3210e-09]  (20000 resamples, seed 12345)
      BCa       95% CI [-4.0214e-08, +7.8329e-09]   (2x the false-promotion rate at n~50 — do not gate on it)
      relative  95% CI [-7.818%, +3.000%]
      studentised   CI [-2.0842e-08, +1.6990e-08]   <- READ THIS ONE (measured at nominal coverage; see coverage_lab)
  SECONDARY  geometric mean of per-MLP ratios (>1 = candidate better)
      gain             1.0221x   95% CI [1.0051, 1.0395]
  candidate better on 49/50   sign-test p = 0.0000
  *** ESTIMANDS DISAGREE: arithmetic says control, geometric says candidate. The competition is arithmetic. ***

    mechanism: the candidate improves 49/50 MLPs by 3% and regresses one by 49%.
    The geometric mean weights every MLP's LOG equally, so a single tail blow-up is
    invisible to it. The competition sums scores, so that one MLP is 7.2% of the objective.

